  "id": "COMPOUND:21079 - PROTEIN:5569",
  "verbalization": "Palmarumycin CP18 is implicated in the regulation of HEK-293T cells through multiple indirect pathways. The drug is predicted to act as a target on Bromodomain-containing protein 4, which is a known target of Patupilone, and also on A704, which targets 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn targets HEK-293T. Similarly, palmarumycin CP18 is predicted to interact with HPAF-II, which targets a compound that also targets HEK-293T. These pathways collectively suggest that palmarumycin CP18 influences HEK-293T through a series of molecular interactions, likely by modulating the activity of proteins involved in cellular processes that ultimately affect the cell's behavior. The integration of these targets highlights a potential mechanism by which palmarumycin CP18 may exert its effects on HEK-293T, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
